    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This introduction section discusses the significant role of early affiliative experiences in physical and psychological well-being, highlighting how both positive and negative early emotional memories influence human development and vulnerability to psychopathology. It explores the concept of social safeness and its association with psychopathological indicators, and introduces body appreciation as a positive, accepting attitude towards one's body. The section concludes by stating the aim of the current study, which is to test an integrative model exploring the impact of early memories of warmth and safeness on eating psychopathology, mediated by social safeness and body appreciation.",
